---
title: Lemon Curd
yield: 1%litre
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

Sterilise #3 × 350 ml jars{} in very hot soapy water or in the hot cycle of the dishwasher. Place the jars onto a baking tray and slide into an oven set to 160°C for 10 to ~{15%minutes}.

Lightly whisk the @eggs{4%large} in a #medium-sized saucepan{}, then add the rest of the ingredients (@lemons{4%large juicy}(grated zest and juice), @caster sugar{350%g}, @unsalted butter{225%g}(at room temperature, cut into small lumps), and @cornflour{2%tsp}) and place the saucepan over a medium heat. Whisk continuously using a balloon whisk until the mixture thickens; about 7 to ~{8%minutes}. Alternatively whisk the eggs using the food processor blades on speed 5, and then use the flexible beater at 90°C on stir speed 1.

Lower the heat to its minimum setting and let the curd gently simmer for a further ~{1%minute}, continuing to whisk.

Remove from the heat. Now pour the lemon curd into the hot, sterilised jars, filling them as full as possible, cover straightaway with waxed discs, and seal while it is still hot.

> It will keep for several weeks, but it must be stored in a cool place.